0.04: Add a boot-owned accelerometer rest recorder, 10-second quiet confirmation, five-minute levels and a rolling 24-hour outward radial graph on the lunar orbit; configurable level-5 height (1-14 px), quiet threshold and enable switch. Preserve green daytime/yellow nighttime observer line.
0.03: Add optional 30-second solar-eclipse shading: black umbra, dithered penumbra, observer above shadow; separate ephemeris/render modules with lazy tables and conservative screening.
0.02: Color the observer zenith line green by day and yellow by night; check color transitions each minute.
0.01: Release tenkyu under the existing orbit app ID using the refined tenkyu implementation, reorganized settings, configurable Roman hour scale, updated sunrise/sunset rays, reduced display refresh frequency and the new 48x48 globe-and-Moon icon. Default to hidden Roman numerals, date below the Sun, time in the header and Japan / Tokyo / Chiyoda-ku. Use orbit storage/module names without importing standalone tenkyu settings.

